    "q-279714": {
      "dom_id": "step-q279714",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If $X∼B(5,\\frac{2}{3}),$  then, **rounded to $3$ decimal places**, $P(3\\le X<5)≈${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial, we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(5,\\frac{2}{3}),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{5-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{3,4\\}) \\\\  & =f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{3}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{5-3}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{5-4} \\\\  & =10{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{3}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{1} \\\\  & ≈0.658\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
