    "q-281207": {
      "dom_id": "step-q281207",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "If $X∼B(8,0.7),$ then, **rounded to $3$ decimal places**, $P(X\\le 6)≈${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(8,0.7),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{8}{x}){(0.7)}^{x}{(0.3)}^{8-x}.\n$$\n\nComputing $P(X\\le 6)$ will require us to compute $f(x)$ at $x=0,1,2,…,6.$ However, if we compute the complement $P(X>6)$ instead, then we will only have to compute $f(x)$ at $x=7,8,$ which will result in a much faster computation.\n\nComputing $P(X>6),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =P(X\\in \\{7,8\\}) \\\\  & =f(7)+f(8) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{8}{7}){(0.7)}^{7}{(0.3)}^{8-7}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{8}{8}){(0.7)}^{8}{(0.3)}^{8-8} \\\\  & =8{(0.7)}^{7}{(0.3)}^{1}+1{(0.7)}^{8}{(0.3)}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.255\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 6) & =1-P(X>6) \\\\  & ≈1-0.255 \\\\  & =0.745\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
